---
system: sys-03-device-runtime-local-interaction
flow_id: config-pull
surface: device
spec_anchor: /software/systems/03-device-runtime-local-interaction#config-pull-contract
actors: [Device, Gateway, ConfigService, KMS, PostgreSQL]
apis:
  - GET /v1/config/fetch
  - POST /v1/config/applied
externals: [KMS]
queues: []
failure_paths:
  - config_signature_failure
  - config_size_exceeds_8kb
  - schema_version_unsupported_major
  - kms_signing_failure
idempotency: ETag / If-None-Match yields 304 when version matches sys.last_config_etag
retry: device retries on 5xx with backoff; falls back to 6h periodic poll on transient failure
timeout: 5s p99 fetch
status: final
---
%% HAND-CURATED. Device-side verifies ECDSA P-256 signature with embedded public key pair (current_key + next_key) per sys-08.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Device
    participant Gateway
    participant ConfigService
    participant KMS
    participant PostgreSQL

    Device->>Gateway: GET /v1/config/fetch (mTLS) {X-Device-Id, X-Schema-Version-Min/Max, X-Current-Config-Version}
    Gateway->>ConfigService: forward
    alt 304 not_modified
        ConfigService-->>Device: 304 (update sys.last_heartbeat_at only, no state mutation)
    else schema_version_unsupported_major
        ConfigService-->>Device: 412 schema_version_unsupported_major
    else success
        ConfigService->>PostgreSQL: SELECT device_configs WHERE device_id
        PostgreSQL-->>ConfigService: {config_blob, config_signature, config_version, schema_version}
        ConfigService-->>Device: 200 {configVersion, schemaVersion, configSignature, issuedAt, configBlob}
    end

    Device->>Device: reconstruct signing payload from received config
    alt config_signature_failure (both current_key and next_key fail)
        Device->>Device: reject payload, retain previous config, emit config_signature_failure telemetry
    else next_key succeeds
        Device->>Device: accept config + promote next_key to current_key (rotation window)
    else current_key succeeds
        Device->>Device: validate schema, validate size ≤8KB, persist to nvs_policy, publish CONFIG_APPLIED
    end

    Device->>Gateway: POST /v1/config/applied {device_id, configVersion} (mTLS)
    Gateway->>ConfigService: forward
    ConfigService->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE device_configs SET applied_at=now()
    PostgreSQL-->>ConfigService: ok
    ConfigService-->>Device: 204

    Note over Device,PostgreSQL: timeout 5s p99 · kms_signing_failure / config_size_exceeds_8kb surface as upstream assembly errors (sys-08) · 6h periodic poll catches missed MQTT notifies
